          "parts": [
            "To solve for \\( B \\), we start with the equation:\n\n\\[\n1 + A = \\frac{B}{C}\n\\]\n\nWe know:\n- \\( A = 10.0584 \\)\n- \\( C = 0.4725 \\)\n\nRearranging the equation to solve for \\( B \\):\n\n\\[\nB = (1 + A) \\times C\n\\]\n\nNow substitute the known values:\n\n\\[\nB = (1 + 10.0584) \\times 0.4725\n\\]\n\n\\[\nB = 11.0584 \\times 0.4725\n\\]\n\nNow, let's calculate that.\n\n\\[\nB = 5.2305\n\\]\n\nSo, the value of \\( B \\) is approximately \\( 5.2305 \\)."
          ]
